# BoardQuest — line-ending policy
#
# Backend (Render) and CI run on Linux: text files must be LF in the
# repository and in every checkout. This file makes that true regardless of
# each developer's local core.autocrlf setting (no per-machine config needed).
#
#   text=auto  -> Git normalizes text files to LF on commit
#   eol=lf     -> Git checks text files out with LF (even on Windows)

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Windows-only scripts keep CRLF (cmd.exe batch files require it) --------
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# --- Binary assets: never normalize (future-proofing) -----------------------
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.wasm binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
